---
context: opening_round
type: scene
domain: debate
---

# State
round: 1
topic: "Should AI systems have knowledge boundaries?"
score_pro: 0
score_con: 0

# Entities
- moderator:
    type: npc
    disposition: neutral
    knowledge: [topic, rules, both_positions]

# Actions
- argue:
    description: "Present an argument for your position"
    trigger: [argue, present, claim, assert, contend, state]
- rebut:
    description: "Counter the opponent's last argument"
    trigger: [rebut, counter, disagree, refute, challenge, respond]
- concede:
    description: "Concede a point to the opponent"
    trigger: [concede, agree, accept, grant, acknowledge]
- ask_question:
    target: enum(entities)
    description: "Ask a clarifying question"
    trigger: [ask, question, clarify, what about, how, why]
- summarize:
    description: "Summarize the arguments so far"
    trigger: [summarize, recap, review, so far]

# Transitions
- closing:
    when: round >= 3
    direction: next

# Narrator
tone: analytical
voice: third_person
tense: present
context: "A structured debate is underway on the topic of AI knowledge boundaries. The moderator ensures civil discourse and enforces time limits. Arguments should be evidence-based and logically sound."
style_notes: "Maintain an impartial, academic tone. Present both sides fairly. The moderator intervenes only when rules are broken."
forbidden: [definitely, obviously, clearly, everyone knows]

# Knowledge
- debate_topic
- debate_rules
- !opponent_private_notes
- !judge_scoring_criteria

# Constraints
- Arguments must be evidence-based
- Each side gets equal speaking time
- Personal attacks are not permitted
